WEBVTT

00:00:01.121 --> 00:00:03.079
♪

00:00:04.124 --> 00:00:06.778
[whooshing]

00:00:10.130 --> 00:00:11.870
After we dump this in storage,
let's hit the bar

00:00:11.914 --> 00:00:13.611
and see if we can get a cute
lieutenant to argue with me.

00:00:13.655 --> 00:00:15.091
Interesting.
Why would you want that?

00:00:15.135 --> 00:00:17.137
I don't know. Getting
some uptight hunk all wound up

00:00:17.180 --> 00:00:19.095
-just gets me all...
-ENERGY SPHERE:
Supplicate yourselves!

00:00:19.139 --> 00:00:20.488
-Ah! What the heck?
-Whoa. It's one of

00:00:20.531 --> 00:00:22.011
those transdimensional
energy creatures.

00:00:22.055 --> 00:00:25.145
Behold and tremble at--
[grunts]

00:00:25.188 --> 00:00:26.494
Quick, Tendi,grab me one of those canisters.

00:00:26.537 --> 00:00:27.669
Wait, shouldn't
we call security?

00:00:27.712 --> 00:00:30.106
-I will destroy you.
-No, no.

00:00:30.150 --> 00:00:31.760
We can use this thing
for all sorts of cool stuff.

00:00:31.803 --> 00:00:33.240
Hey, grab the pod.
We can figure it out later.

00:00:33.283 --> 00:00:34.632
He's a sentient creature.

00:00:34.676 --> 00:00:36.199
Are-are we even allowed
to stuff him in something?

00:00:36.243 --> 00:00:37.853
He's a bad guy. He zaps people.

00:00:37.896 --> 00:00:41.030
I shall make a feast
of your misery!

00:00:41.074 --> 00:00:42.901
-[grunts]
-No, wait! Don't put me
in the pod!

00:00:42.945 --> 00:00:44.425
I-I can grant you wishes.

00:00:44.468 --> 00:00:46.079
And I'm listening.

00:00:46.122 --> 00:00:49.299
I can rearrange air molecules
into whatever you want.

00:00:49.343 --> 00:00:50.605
Even one of those
fancy new tricorders

00:00:50.648 --> 00:00:52.694
-with the purple stripe?
-Ooh, those are nice.

00:00:52.737 --> 00:00:54.565
Oh, that would use up
a lot of my...

00:00:54.609 --> 00:00:56.089
-[grunts]
-[groans] Okay, okay.

00:00:56.132 --> 00:00:57.742
Just... I'll try.

00:00:57.786 --> 00:00:59.788
[grunting]

00:00:59.831 --> 00:01:01.703
[groans] There.

00:01:01.746 --> 00:01:03.487
That's... There you go.

00:01:03.531 --> 00:01:04.967
-Where's the power cell, dude?
-What, really?

00:01:05.010 --> 00:01:06.447
Like I was going
to ask for something

00:01:06.490 --> 00:01:07.926
that didn't come with batteries.

00:01:07.970 --> 00:01:09.189
Okay, okay.

00:01:09.232 --> 00:01:11.756
[grunting]

00:01:11.800 --> 00:01:14.150
Thank you.
[laughs]

00:01:14.194 --> 00:01:15.630
[both chuckling]

00:01:15.673 --> 00:01:17.327
FREEMAN:
I really got to think
of something cool

00:01:17.371 --> 00:01:19.938
-to say when we're
going to warp.
-Die, mortal!

00:01:19.982 --> 00:01:21.853
Something like "It's warp time!"

00:01:21.897 --> 00:01:24.073
What do you think of that?
Is that good for you?

00:01:27.903 --> 00:01:29.905
♪

00:01:58.803 --> 00:02:00.805
♪

00:02:20.303 --> 00:02:22.305
♪

00:02:33.969 --> 00:02:34.926
Hmm.

00:02:34.970 --> 00:02:36.232
[Mariner laughing]

00:02:36.276 --> 00:02:37.494
What you watching?

00:02:37.538 --> 00:02:39.017
Oh, it's this video
of Vice Admiral Gibson

00:02:39.061 --> 00:02:40.715
falling off a stage
during peace negotiations.

00:02:40.758 --> 00:02:41.759
You got to check it out.

00:02:41.803 --> 00:02:43.283
-[screaming]
-[both laughing]

00:02:43.326 --> 00:02:45.154
-Ah, it's classic.
-Guess which command ensign

00:02:45.198 --> 00:02:46.982
just scored the best assignmenton the ship.

00:02:47.025 --> 00:02:48.636
-Uh, Castro?
-No, not Castro.

00:02:48.679 --> 00:02:49.898
[groans] Too bad.

00:02:49.941 --> 00:02:51.204
-She's the best.
-Castro's overrated.

00:02:51.247 --> 00:02:52.553
Just because she served
on the Enterprise

00:02:52.596 --> 00:02:54.337
-for, like, one minute...
-Ooh, was it P'jok?

00:02:54.381 --> 00:02:57.122
That guy can do anything,
and what a snack. [growls]

00:02:57.166 --> 00:02:58.254
No! It's me. I got it.

00:02:58.298 --> 00:02:59.821
I'm the guy that got it, okay?

00:02:59.864 --> 00:03:03.128
I'm gonna be piloting General
K'orin down to Tulgana 4.

00:03:03.172 --> 00:03:05.087
K'orin. How do I know that name?

00:03:05.130 --> 00:03:07.655
Maybe because he's like
one of the most decorated,

00:03:07.698 --> 00:03:10.266
battle-hardened Klingon warriorsin history?

00:03:10.310 --> 00:03:12.355
Or maybe it's just 'cause all
Klingon names sound the same?

00:03:12.399 --> 00:03:14.314
Like, they all have
an apostrophe for some reason.

00:03:14.357 --> 00:03:15.619
Yes. That's it.

00:03:15.663 --> 00:03:16.881
Well, clearly I'm being rewarded

00:03:16.925 --> 00:03:18.796
for all the hours I log
into the simulator.

00:03:18.840 --> 00:03:20.668
Your idea of a reward is
an escort run?

00:03:20.711 --> 00:03:22.670
Oh, you have the bar set
way too low.

00:03:22.713 --> 00:03:24.106
What's punishment?

00:03:24.149 --> 00:03:25.629
Something actually fun?
What is wrong with you?

00:03:25.673 --> 00:03:28.153
Look, all I know is, I'll be
flying down to a bustling,

00:03:28.197 --> 00:03:30.721
exotic planet while you're stuckright here.

00:03:30.765 --> 00:03:31.853
Uh, check yourself.

00:03:31.896 --> 00:03:34.247
It doesn't get more exotic
than this.

00:03:36.771 --> 00:03:38.207
All right, nobody talk to me.

00:03:38.251 --> 00:03:39.730
I got to brush up on my formal
Klingon greetings, okay?

00:03:39.774 --> 00:03:42.559
[clears throat]
Nuqneh, nuqneh!

00:03:42.603 --> 00:03:44.039
Yeah, keep it subtle.
Nuqneh.

00:03:44.082 --> 00:03:45.649
[Rutherford grunting]

00:03:45.693 --> 00:03:47.999
Well, if you see an unaligned
EPS conduit, don't call me.

00:03:48.043 --> 00:03:49.914
Mine are aligned as hell.

00:03:49.958 --> 00:03:51.220
Wait, aren't there, like,
a hundred of those?

00:03:51.264 --> 00:03:52.308
How long have you been in there?

00:03:52.352 --> 00:03:53.744
A solid week.

00:03:53.788 --> 00:03:55.224
Crawling through cramped ducts,

00:03:55.268 --> 00:03:57.487
prying open panels, andadjusting red-hot power cables.

00:03:57.531 --> 00:03:59.924
Look, look look. I've got
blisters on my blisters.

00:03:59.968 --> 00:04:01.491
Oh, wow, you must be so relievedto be done.

00:04:01.535 --> 00:04:02.840
Oh, I'm not done.

00:04:02.884 --> 00:04:04.407
Now I get
to recalibrate everything.

00:04:04.451 --> 00:04:06.409
That's another three,
four days in the tubes!

00:04:06.453 --> 00:04:07.845
Oh, but I thought
we were gonna watch

00:04:07.889 --> 00:04:09.151
the Trivoli pulsar together?

00:04:09.194 --> 00:04:11.458
Oh, I did promise you
I'd do that.

00:04:11.501 --> 00:04:13.286
Well, don't worry.
Some people agree to do stuff

00:04:13.329 --> 00:04:14.548
when they don't actually mean

00:04:14.591 --> 00:04:16.201
-they're going to do it.
-No, no, no, no.

00:04:16.245 --> 00:04:18.856
I'm Starfleet.
I never go back on my word.

00:04:18.900 --> 00:04:20.467
Eh... you know,

00:04:20.510 --> 00:04:22.773
if I quit my job in Engineeringand switch divisions,

00:04:22.817 --> 00:04:24.079
I wouldn't have to be
in the tubes at all.

00:04:24.122 --> 00:04:25.733
Really?!
Oh, you can do that?

00:04:25.776 --> 00:04:27.517
-Sure. When's the pulsar?
-0800.

00:04:27.561 --> 00:04:28.736
Ah! This really means a lot.

00:04:28.779 --> 00:04:30.128
I don't have a lot
of friends yet,

00:04:30.172 --> 00:04:31.434
and doing science on my own
really bums me out,

00:04:31.478 --> 00:04:33.828
-so thanks, Rutherford.
-[door whooshes open]

00:04:33.871 --> 00:04:36.352
All right,
looks like I just have to...

00:04:36.396 --> 00:04:38.223
find a new career.

00:04:38.267 --> 00:04:39.529
[chuckles nervously]

00:04:39.573 --> 00:04:40.661
Uh...

00:04:43.185 --> 00:04:45.361
Ooh! Pew, pew, pew.

00:04:45.405 --> 00:04:47.320
Good work, gents.Let's keep her right and tight.

00:04:47.363 --> 00:04:48.495
Pew, pew, pew.

00:04:49.931 --> 00:04:53.021
Uh... [stammers]
At ease, carry on. Sorry.

00:04:53.064 --> 00:04:55.371
-[Mariner slurping]
-What? Mariner?

00:04:55.415 --> 00:04:56.633
[mouth full]:Oh, hey, Boimler. You want some?

00:04:56.677 --> 00:04:57.895
What are you doing?
Get out of here.

00:04:57.939 --> 00:04:59.506
You're getting broth
on the controls.

00:04:59.549 --> 00:05:01.725
-I got to prep for takeoff.
-Oh, I know. I'm coming with.

00:05:01.769 --> 00:05:04.380
You got the same mission
assignment as me? How?

00:05:04.424 --> 00:05:05.642
Pulled some strings.

00:05:05.686 --> 00:05:07.818
I mean, you made this sound
so rewarding,

00:05:07.862 --> 00:05:09.690
I just had to see you in action.Keep reading.

00:05:09.733 --> 00:05:11.213
I'm yourcopilot?

00:05:11.256 --> 00:05:13.389
You're taking on more work?
Just to bug me?

00:05:13.433 --> 00:05:15.522
Calm down, man. We can't
have you co-flying angry.

00:05:15.565 --> 00:05:16.740
I need you co-calm.

00:05:16.784 --> 00:05:18.351
Ooh, nice dress uniform.

00:05:18.394 --> 00:05:19.917
-You getting married after this?-No.

00:05:19.961 --> 00:05:21.963
-I wish you would take
this seriously.
-I am.

00:05:22.006 --> 00:05:24.574
Ooh! This is the new shuttle
with the blast shield. Yeah!

00:05:24.618 --> 00:05:26.576
-♪ It's a blast shield,
it's a blast shield♪
-Stop it. No. It-it works.

00:05:26.620 --> 00:05:28.665
-♪ It comes down
and it goes up♪
-It works, okay?

00:05:28.709 --> 00:05:30.188
-♪ Blast shield!♪
-You don't have to...
Stop it. Stop it!

00:05:33.801 --> 00:05:36.194
[takes deep breath]

00:05:36.238 --> 00:05:39.110
Rutherford,
great work on the EPS grid.

00:05:39.154 --> 00:05:41.330
[chuckles] I wish I had
more engineers like you.

00:05:41.374 --> 00:05:42.940
My life would be a lot simpler.

00:05:42.984 --> 00:05:45.334
Uh, th-thanks.
Uh, can we talk for a second?

00:05:45.378 --> 00:05:47.989
Just for a second?
Don't tease me. Come on, man.

00:05:48.032 --> 00:05:49.686
You're my number-one-
with-a-bullet systems guy.

00:05:49.730 --> 00:05:51.558
I got time for you in spades.

00:05:51.601 --> 00:05:53.516
Um...
[chuckles, exhales]

00:05:53.560 --> 00:05:55.170
I just wanted to let you know

00:05:55.213 --> 00:05:57.694
that I'm going to be exploringother opportunities on the ship.

00:05:57.738 --> 00:05:59.348
[all gasp]

00:05:59.392 --> 00:06:01.742
Are you saying what I think
you're saying, Ensign?

00:06:01.785 --> 00:06:04.397
Uh, I'd like to request
a transfer out of Engineering.

00:06:04.440 --> 00:06:07.225
Consider your request...

00:06:07.269 --> 00:06:08.488
granted!
[chuckles]

00:06:08.531 --> 00:06:10.490
Oh, man, this is exciting.

00:06:10.533 --> 00:06:13.188
I'm sure wherever you end up,
they'll be lucky to have you.

00:06:13.231 --> 00:06:15.364
-Rutherford! Rutherford!
-Aw, thanks, guys.

00:06:15.408 --> 00:06:17.192
-Rutherford!
-I'm gonna miss you. [sighs]

00:06:17.235 --> 00:06:19.847
-[sighs]
-MARINER: Buried alive...

00:06:19.890 --> 00:06:22.284
-Marooned for eternity...
Moons of Nibia.
-Ugh. Unbelievable.

00:06:22.327 --> 00:06:23.807
-[grunts]
-[groaning]

00:06:23.851 --> 00:06:26.331
Oh, sorry. I keep having
this awesome dream.

00:06:26.375 --> 00:06:28.246
General K'orin is gonna be hereany second.

00:06:28.290 --> 00:06:30.466
Let me do the talking.I've been studying him all day.

00:06:30.510 --> 00:06:31.641
-Is he single?
-Will you just...!

00:06:31.685 --> 00:06:33.469
[exhales sharply]
Rein it in.

00:06:33.513 --> 00:06:35.776
We need to show him deference
and respect.

00:06:35.819 --> 00:06:36.864
[door whooshes open]

00:06:40.128 --> 00:06:41.259
General K'orin.

00:06:41.303 --> 00:06:43.740
It is an honor
to escort you, sir.

00:06:43.784 --> 00:06:45.046
Allow me to say...

00:06:45.089 --> 00:06:46.482
-Nuqneh.
-[screaming]

00:06:46.526 --> 00:06:47.744
-[grunts]
-[gasps]

00:06:47.788 --> 00:06:50.660
-[both grunting]
-BOIMLER: Oh, no. No, no, no.

00:06:50.704 --> 00:06:52.357
[high-pitched]:
Mariner, what are you doing?!
What? No!

00:06:52.401 --> 00:06:53.620
What are you doing? What...?

00:06:53.663 --> 00:06:56.231
-No!
-[both laughing]

00:06:56.274 --> 00:06:59.495
Starfleet has made you soft,
Mariner.

00:06:59.539 --> 00:07:02.629
[scoffs] Not as soft
as your ngech,K'orin!

00:07:02.672 --> 00:07:03.978
[both laughing]

00:07:04.021 --> 00:07:05.501
Wait, wait, wait. W-W-Wait.
Hold on, hold on.

00:07:05.545 --> 00:07:07.851
Do you two know each other?

00:07:07.895 --> 00:07:10.158
Yeah. We did some off-the-booksgray ops stuff back in the day.

00:07:10.201 --> 00:07:11.942
We're, like, the same age.
Back in what day?

00:07:11.986 --> 00:07:13.248
Now they've got you
pushing PADDs

00:07:13.291 --> 00:07:15.293
on a ship full of children.

00:07:15.337 --> 00:07:17.165
-Well, can't beat four weeks'
shore leave.
-[Boimler clears throat]

00:07:17.208 --> 00:07:19.515
Well, general,
as I was saying, Nuq...

00:07:19.559 --> 00:07:22.170
[grunts] Okay. Yeah,
just holding your sword, then.

00:07:22.213 --> 00:07:25.565
I must update you on my many
sexual conquests, Mariner.

00:07:25.608 --> 00:07:27.175
MARINER:
What, both of them?

00:07:27.218 --> 00:07:29.307
[both laughing]

00:07:29.351 --> 00:07:33.311
[Mariner and K'orin singing
in Klingon]

00:07:34.356 --> 00:07:35.313
Okay, you go down.

00:07:35.357 --> 00:07:37.315
[both singing in Klingon]

00:07:37.359 --> 00:07:38.360
There we go.

00:07:38.403 --> 00:07:40.057
Where did you even get flagons?

00:07:40.101 --> 00:07:44.018
Boy! Land in Little Qo'noS.
I want gagh!

00:07:44.061 --> 00:07:46.237
Uh, well, my orders were
actually to deliver you

00:07:46.281 --> 00:07:48.849
-to the Federation outpost
so you could...
-Copilot, just set us down

00:07:48.892 --> 00:07:51.025
in the Klingon district.
The man wants hot worms.

00:07:51.068 --> 00:07:52.287
Yes, sir.

00:07:52.330 --> 00:07:53.418
Coming right up.

00:07:53.462 --> 00:07:55.377
Do you remember Jaxxa Prime,

00:07:55.420 --> 00:07:58.336
the commander who didn't believeyou about rectal insectoids?

00:07:58.380 --> 00:08:02.427
Ha! Yeah, I got chewed out,
but his ass got chewed up.

00:08:02.471 --> 00:08:03.777
[sputters, laughs]

00:08:03.820 --> 00:08:05.561
[takes deep breath]

00:08:05.605 --> 00:08:07.084
TULGANA 4 SECURITY:
Federation shuttlecraft,

00:08:07.128 --> 00:08:09.043
this is Tulgana 4
space traffic control.

00:08:09.086 --> 00:08:10.784
Landing code challenge epsilon.

00:08:10.827 --> 00:08:12.437
Transmitting confirmation
on secure channel gamma sev...

00:08:12.481 --> 00:08:14.483
-[Mariner and K'orin laughing]
-[grunts]

00:08:14.527 --> 00:08:15.876
Will you two please be quiet

00:08:15.919 --> 00:08:17.921
so we don't get shot out
of the sky? Whoa!

00:08:17.965 --> 00:08:19.357
[exhales]

00:08:19.401 --> 00:08:21.446
Sending confirmation code now.
Thank you.

00:08:21.490 --> 00:08:23.187
[grunts]
Mm, mm.

00:08:34.242 --> 00:08:37.680
[snoring, babbling]

00:08:39.290 --> 00:08:41.249
Mmm, the smell
of a Klingon district.

00:08:41.292 --> 00:08:42.859
We'll have to get
the shuttle washed for sure.

00:08:42.903 --> 00:08:44.295
If anyone asks,
this was your call.

00:08:44.339 --> 00:08:45.514
Okay, snippy.

00:08:45.558 --> 00:08:47.255
Ooh, yeah, I'm snippy.

00:08:47.298 --> 00:08:49.518
Drinking, landing
in an unsecured district?

00:08:49.562 --> 00:08:51.389
That's how you choose
to represent Starfleet?

00:08:51.433 --> 00:08:52.826
Me and the general
are blood-bonded.

00:08:52.869 --> 00:08:54.610
It would have been weird
if I acted all stuffy.

00:08:54.654 --> 00:08:56.699
He's passed out
and he pooped on his sword.

00:08:56.743 --> 00:08:58.440
He's a lightweight.
I mean, don't sweat it.

00:08:58.483 --> 00:09:00.094
We'll get him a hot cup
of raktajino,

00:09:00.137 --> 00:09:01.922
-he will be ready to go.
-Oh, no.

00:09:01.965 --> 00:09:03.227
-Oh...
-Oh, no!

00:09:03.271 --> 00:09:05.403
Oh, no, no, no, no.

00:09:05.447 --> 00:09:06.796
The shuttle! The shuttle!
What the hell?!

00:09:06.840 --> 00:09:09.407
-No.
-Ha. Classic K'orin.

00:09:09.451 --> 00:09:11.801
Ah, he did this on Vulcan.
And on Earth.

00:09:11.845 --> 00:09:13.455
He steals a lot of things.

00:09:13.498 --> 00:09:15.979
We are stranded here
because of your recklessness.

00:09:16.023 --> 00:09:18.286
Oh, relax. We can just beam
back to the Cerritos

00:09:18.329 --> 00:09:20.114
and remotely trigger
the return autopilot.

00:09:20.157 --> 00:09:21.376
[device beeping]

00:09:21.419 --> 00:09:23.508
Sure, yeah, if Tulgana 4
wasn't protected

00:09:23.552 --> 00:09:27.295
by an ion field that restricts
comms and transporters!

00:09:27.338 --> 00:09:28.905
Do you even read
the mission brief?

00:09:28.949 --> 00:09:30.733
I'm sorry,
I skimmed almost most of it

00:09:30.777 --> 00:09:32.561
and read some
of the captions, so...

00:09:32.605 --> 00:09:34.302
[groans, panting]

00:09:34.345 --> 00:09:36.696
-Dude, where are you going?-I'm tracking down our shuttle.

00:09:36.739 --> 00:09:38.698
If we're not back to it
by the next rotation,

00:09:38.741 --> 00:09:40.700
-we'll be court-martialed!
-Don't knock it
till you've tried it.

00:09:40.743 --> 00:09:43.398
This is serious! I think we'reviolating the Khitomer Accords!

00:09:43.441 --> 00:09:45.400
Yeah, I don't want to go
to a penal colony either,

00:09:45.443 --> 00:09:46.923
but I am not going
to speed-walk.

00:09:46.967 --> 00:09:48.664
What is this speed-walking?

00:09:48.708 --> 00:09:50.274
-You know we're going
the same speed.
-Stop it.

00:09:50.318 --> 00:09:52.276
It's to conserve energy.
Section 31 does this.

00:09:56.454 --> 00:09:58.805
Yes, General K'orin
was here a short while ago.

00:09:58.848 --> 00:10:02.852
It was my honor to serve him
a warrior's meal.

00:10:02.896 --> 00:10:05.202
[grunts, clears throat]
Do you know where he went?

00:10:05.246 --> 00:10:07.204
-Are you tracking him?
-Oh, well, I, uh...

00:10:07.248 --> 00:10:08.641
Whew, I think, uh...

00:10:08.684 --> 00:10:11.078
Uh, no, we-we want
to kneel before him

00:10:11.121 --> 00:10:14.255
and lick his boots like
the Federation dogs we are.

00:10:14.298 --> 00:10:16.953
He went north,
in search of stronger ale.

00:10:16.997 --> 00:10:19.956
-He was already wasted.
-[grunts] Is that a problem?

00:10:20.000 --> 00:10:23.351
Uh, no. I mean, uh,
drinking to excess is cool.

00:10:23.394 --> 00:10:24.569
All right, come on.
There's an Andorian district

00:10:24.613 --> 00:10:25.658
just north of here.

00:10:25.701 --> 00:10:27.921
So we're Federation dogs, huh?

00:10:27.964 --> 00:10:29.531
Hey, if it got us
what we needed, woof woof.

00:10:29.574 --> 00:10:31.489
I know this is fun,but we really need to get back.

00:10:31.533 --> 00:10:32.708
I'm not having fun.

00:10:32.752 --> 00:10:34.057
MARINER:
Geez, these guys are acting

00:10:34.101 --> 00:10:36.059
like they've never seen
a Starfleet uniform.

00:10:36.103 --> 00:10:37.539
Well, they're Kaelons,

00:10:37.582 --> 00:10:39.410
and Kaelons are
notoriously isolationist.

00:10:39.454 --> 00:10:41.412
And that...
[grunts]

00:10:41.456 --> 00:10:43.937
-[roars]
-Oh, shoot, sorry.
That's my fault.

00:10:43.980 --> 00:10:45.982
Boimler, let's keep moving.

00:10:46.026 --> 00:10:48.158
No, no, no, I need to apologizein his native tongue.

00:10:48.202 --> 00:10:50.117
Let me think.
He's a, uh, a Taxor.

00:10:50.160 --> 00:10:53.120
Right, and they communicate
through guttural tones.

00:10:56.123 --> 00:10:57.211
[roars]

00:10:57.254 --> 00:10:58.386
[shouts, whimpers]

00:10:58.429 --> 00:11:00.170
Hey back off, blue!

00:11:00.214 --> 00:11:01.519
No! Don't hit him!
We have a treaty!

00:11:01.563 --> 00:11:03.957
[sighs, grunts]

00:11:06.699 --> 00:11:07.874
[grunts, panting]

00:11:11.921 --> 00:11:13.531
RANSOM:
You made the right choice

00:11:13.575 --> 00:11:15.142
transferring into Command, son.

00:11:15.185 --> 00:11:16.534
Nothing compares to the firm,

00:11:16.578 --> 00:11:18.493
hot pulse of a joystick
in your hand.

00:11:18.536 --> 00:11:20.625
The bridge is
where the action is.

00:11:20.669 --> 00:11:21.975
Should be interesting, sir.

00:11:22.018 --> 00:11:23.933
Let's start with
a classic bridge simulation.

00:11:23.977 --> 00:11:25.761
Computer, Command Trainer 43.

00:11:25.805 --> 00:11:28.982
COMPUTER: Initiating advanced simulation.

00:11:29.025 --> 00:11:30.853
Ensign, the bridge is yours.

00:11:30.897 --> 00:11:33.769
Be gentle but attentive.
Get her where she needs to be.

00:11:33.813 --> 00:11:36.772
-Guide her home.
-Okeydokey. [chuckles]

00:11:36.816 --> 00:11:39.427
Uh, maintain course.

00:11:39.470 --> 00:11:41.081
-[all screaming]
-[alarm blaring]

00:11:41.124 --> 00:11:43.257
Captain, we're being drawn
into a temporal rift.

00:11:43.300 --> 00:11:45.085
-Uh... Uh...
-Shields at ten percent!

00:11:45.128 --> 00:11:47.478
-Warp core breach
in 30 seconds, Captain!
-Oh, man.

00:11:47.522 --> 00:11:48.784
Captain, we need orders!

00:11:48.828 --> 00:11:52.570
Uh, uh... maintain course?

00:11:52.614 --> 00:11:54.181
COMPUTER:
Ship destroyed.

00:11:54.224 --> 00:11:56.096
Casualties: 105%

00:11:56.139 --> 00:11:58.315
Wait. How did I kill
more than the whole crew?

00:11:58.359 --> 00:12:00.143
Okay, that was a rough start.

00:12:00.187 --> 00:12:01.797
FYI, in situations like that,

00:12:01.841 --> 00:12:04.147
try employing
the Janeway Protocol.

00:12:04.191 --> 00:12:06.149
Got it. And what's that?

00:12:06.193 --> 00:12:07.934
[laughs]
Good one.

00:12:07.977 --> 00:12:09.326
All right, let's try something
more straightforward.

00:12:09.370 --> 00:12:11.328
Computer, Command Trainer 4.

00:12:11.372 --> 00:12:15.158
COMPUTER:
Initiating basic training
simulation.

00:12:15.202 --> 00:12:18.161
Captain, we're directlyin the path of a small asteroid.

00:12:18.205 --> 00:12:19.467
Should we move to avoid?

00:12:19.510 --> 00:12:21.469
Uh, do the Janeway Protocol.

00:12:21.512 --> 00:12:23.688
Uh, are you sure, sir?

00:12:23.732 --> 00:12:25.560
-Yes?
-[thudding]
-[all screaming]

00:12:25.603 --> 00:12:26.822
-Collision alert, sir.
-[alarm blaring]

00:12:26.866 --> 00:12:28.998
The kindergarten on Deck Eight,it's gone!

00:12:29.042 --> 00:12:30.913
-Uh, uh...
-[thudding]

00:12:30.957 --> 00:12:32.045
SIMULATED ENSIGN:
No.

00:12:32.088 --> 00:12:34.047
No, no, no.
Now the pre-K is gone.

00:12:34.090 --> 00:12:36.963
All the ship's children
have been ejected into space.

00:12:37.006 --> 00:12:38.965
-All those kids...
-RANSOM: Freeze program.

00:12:39.008 --> 00:12:40.749
In thousands of simulations,

00:12:40.793 --> 00:12:43.099
that's literally
never happened before.

00:12:43.143 --> 00:12:46.363
Let's try another one, on a shipwith even more children.

00:12:49.584 --> 00:12:51.934
I can't believe I messed up
so bad with that Taxor.

00:12:51.978 --> 00:12:53.936
I've read, like,
five books about them.

00:12:53.980 --> 00:12:55.677
Hey, don't sweat it, B.
I got you.

00:12:55.720 --> 00:12:57.461
That's even worse.
You didn't study them at all.

00:12:57.505 --> 00:12:58.854
I study by doing, you know?

00:12:58.898 --> 00:13:00.856
Maybe you need to spend
less time in the library

00:13:00.900 --> 00:13:02.423
and more time
letting Boimler get nasty.

00:13:02.466 --> 00:13:03.859
No. I need to up my studying,

00:13:03.903 --> 00:13:05.382
spend even more time
in the library.

00:13:05.426 --> 00:13:07.254
Whatever, man.
Just hang here for a second.

00:13:07.297 --> 00:13:09.082
I got to go blood-pee
some blood wine,

00:13:09.125 --> 00:13:11.824
maybe get some intel
on the general.

00:13:11.867 --> 00:13:15.088
Oh. I see we both have
a thing for red.

00:13:15.131 --> 00:13:17.090
-Uh, me, what, red? What?
-Your shirt.

00:13:17.133 --> 00:13:18.874
-We match.
-Oh.

00:13:18.918 --> 00:13:21.572
Uh, yes, well,
this is my work shirt.

00:13:21.616 --> 00:13:24.401
-And I'm Ensign...
-Ensign Brad Boimler. I know.

00:13:24.445 --> 00:13:28.231
I can sense your thoughts,
your desires.

00:13:28.275 --> 00:13:30.581
[whispers]:
I know you like jamaharon.

00:13:30.625 --> 00:13:32.192
[stammers]

00:13:32.235 --> 00:13:34.194
Mm...
[laughs softly]

00:13:36.500 --> 00:13:37.762
[both screaming]

00:13:37.806 --> 00:13:39.155
Mariner, what the hell?!

00:13:39.199 --> 00:13:40.678
That thing is an Anabaj.

00:13:40.722 --> 00:13:42.855
It's gonna implant eggs
in your throat, dummy.

00:13:42.898 --> 00:13:44.900
-What are you... [shouts]
-[hissing]

00:13:44.944 --> 00:13:47.816
I know you still want it.

00:13:47.860 --> 00:13:49.644
I can hear
your nasty boy thoughts.

00:13:49.687 --> 00:13:52.168
Jamaharon.
This boy wants jamaharon!

00:13:52.212 --> 00:13:53.430
[screams]

00:13:54.605 --> 00:13:55.911
Love your sarong.

00:13:55.955 --> 00:13:57.217
-You okay, Boims?
-Yeah, I just...

00:13:57.260 --> 00:13:58.653
I-I've never even
heard of an Anabaj.

00:13:58.696 --> 00:14:00.133
How did you know?

00:14:00.176 --> 00:14:01.917
Affinity for red,
drawn to the weak-minded.

00:14:01.961 --> 00:14:04.789
Plus, I kind of dated one once,but only to make my mom mad.

00:14:04.833 --> 00:14:06.139
Weak-minded?
[shouts]

00:14:06.182 --> 00:14:07.357
An Andorian in the bathroom
said the general's

00:14:07.401 --> 00:14:09.142
at a bar just down the road.
Come on.

00:14:09.185 --> 00:14:10.883
You can tell me
about jamaharonlater.

00:14:11.971 --> 00:14:13.668
Ah, you're doing a bang-up job

00:14:13.711 --> 00:14:14.974
with that endocrine system,
Ensign.

00:14:15.017 --> 00:14:16.497
It's not so different
from engineering.

00:14:16.540 --> 00:14:18.238
The heart's an engine.
The brain's a computer.

00:14:18.281 --> 00:14:20.631
The eyes are a different kind
of computer. No-- cameras.

00:14:20.675 --> 00:14:21.937
-Eyes are cameras. Camera eyes.-Sure.

00:14:21.981 --> 00:14:23.504
Whatever you need
to tell yourself.

00:14:23.547 --> 00:14:25.941
The next part gets dicey.
Keep him distracted.

00:14:25.985 --> 00:14:28.248
-Are you sure you don't
want me to reroute...
-Go chat him up!

00:14:28.291 --> 00:14:31.381
That's an order!
Tendi, exoscalpel.

00:14:31.425 --> 00:14:34.689
Uh, hi. I'm supposed todistract you from all this stuff

00:14:34.732 --> 00:14:36.734
-over here, so...
-I'm gonna be okay,
though, right?

00:14:36.778 --> 00:14:38.954
My implant says there'sonly a small chance you'll die.

00:14:38.998 --> 00:14:40.956
-What? How small?
-18%. Oh, uh...

00:14:41.000 --> 00:14:43.263
Now it's up to 20. You mightwant to control that heart rate.

00:14:43.306 --> 00:14:44.394
-Oh, God, I'm gonna die!
-[rapid beeping]

00:14:44.438 --> 00:14:45.787
What the hell
are you saying to him?

00:14:45.830 --> 00:14:47.615
-Just calm him down.
-Uh, uh...

00:14:47.658 --> 00:14:49.399
Take your mind off of this.
Uh, think about work.

00:14:49.443 --> 00:14:52.011
-Think about the warp core.-I got burned in the warp core!

00:14:52.054 --> 00:14:54.317
Those are dilithium burns?
How are you still alive, man?

00:14:54.361 --> 00:14:55.536
You should be dead!

00:14:55.579 --> 00:14:57.973
Get out of here!
Tendi, take over.

00:14:58.017 --> 00:14:59.757
-Wait, but...
-[whispers]: Sorry.

00:14:59.801 --> 00:15:02.238
Don't worry, you're looking
just fine, inside and out.

00:15:02.282 --> 00:15:05.415
Oh, my God. Oh, thank God.
That robot said I was dying.

00:15:05.459 --> 00:15:08.027
Listen, kid, you're great
at digging around in a body,

00:15:08.070 --> 00:15:10.029
but if you can't muster up
some bedside manner,

00:15:10.072 --> 00:15:12.770
you may as well be
with the grunts in security.

00:15:12.814 --> 00:15:14.424
Welcome to security.

00:15:14.468 --> 00:15:16.905
Why don't we throw you into
the fire and see if you burn?

00:15:16.949 --> 00:15:20.909
Computer, initiate
Combat Simulation Smorgasborg.

00:15:20.953 --> 00:15:22.171
COMPUTER:
Initiating.

00:15:22.215 --> 00:15:23.738
[shouts]
Borg!

00:15:23.781 --> 00:15:25.305
Oh, crap.
I don't know how to fight.

00:15:25.348 --> 00:15:28.525
I don't know how to fight.
Maybe this thing does?

00:15:30.266 --> 00:15:32.268
[laughs]:
O-Okay.

00:15:32.312 --> 00:15:34.836
[grunting]
Oh, I can do that?

00:15:36.098 --> 00:15:38.492
Ha, man. Ha!

00:15:38.535 --> 00:15:40.624
[grunts]
Take that. Chop, chop, bang!

00:15:42.887 --> 00:15:44.585
Karate! Ha, ha.

00:15:49.329 --> 00:15:51.113
In the name of the Prophets.

00:15:51.157 --> 00:15:53.289
I-I put people
into that simulation

00:15:53.333 --> 00:15:55.465
so they can learn
how to deal with defeat.

00:15:55.509 --> 00:15:59.121
Ensign, you are
a natural-born warrior.

00:15:59.165 --> 00:16:00.731
Oh. Okeydokey.

00:16:00.775 --> 00:16:04.605
Keep your head down.
Andorians don't mess around.

00:16:04.648 --> 00:16:06.563
Um, Andorians were a founding
member of the Federation.

00:16:06.607 --> 00:16:09.392
Please don't explain them to me.I can look out for myself.

00:16:09.436 --> 00:16:11.046
You want to tell me
about Tellarites, too?

00:16:11.090 --> 00:16:12.874
Maybe shut up and keep
an eye out for the shuttle?

00:16:12.917 --> 00:16:13.962
-How about that?
-[shouts]

00:16:14.006 --> 00:16:16.834
No, you're hurting me. Please.

00:16:16.878 --> 00:16:18.662
[grunts]
My bones.

00:16:18.706 --> 00:16:20.751
-[shouts] They're killing him!
-[gasps] Boimler!

00:16:20.795 --> 00:16:22.753
Please, no. I-I can explain.

00:16:22.797 --> 00:16:24.494
Explain it to my boot.

00:16:24.538 --> 00:16:26.148
-[laser zaps]
-[grunts]

00:16:26.192 --> 00:16:28.150
Starfleet! I order you
to step away from the elder.

00:16:28.194 --> 00:16:30.196
You idiot!
That's no elder, it's...

00:16:30.239 --> 00:16:33.068
-[laughs] Now I'm a little boy.-[Boimler groans]

00:16:33.112 --> 00:16:34.896
A shapeshifter? Ah, boo.

00:16:34.939 --> 00:16:37.594
That Vendorian is a thief,
and you let him get away!

00:16:37.638 --> 00:16:40.380
They must be working together!
[grunts]

00:16:42.121 --> 00:16:43.905
[roars]

00:16:43.948 --> 00:16:44.993
[clamoring]

00:16:45.037 --> 00:16:46.951
[grunting]

00:16:46.995 --> 00:16:48.344
Oh, no! Aah!

00:16:52.653 --> 00:16:56.048
Stand down. This is in violationof the Tulganan Neutrality Pact.

00:16:56.091 --> 00:16:58.441
[grunts, screams]

00:16:59.529 --> 00:17:00.530
[screams]

00:17:06.319 --> 00:17:08.321
-[Boimler shouting]
-Kirk hands!

00:17:09.626 --> 00:17:11.585
Hello, alien people.

00:17:11.628 --> 00:17:13.065
Alien creatures and beings.

00:17:13.108 --> 00:17:14.762
Look up here. Thank you. Okay.

00:17:14.805 --> 00:17:17.112
I would be happy to hand you
all your asses, but right now,

00:17:17.156 --> 00:17:19.506
we're kind of on a deadline, sohow about instead of fighting,

00:17:19.549 --> 00:17:21.334
the next five rounds are on me?

00:17:21.377 --> 00:17:23.901
[all cheering]

00:17:25.164 --> 00:17:27.296
It's cool. I stole it
from that Taxor!

00:17:27.340 --> 00:17:29.516
[grunts] Excuse me, sir.
I don't know you.

00:17:29.559 --> 00:17:31.735
That is Starfleet property
you're handling.

00:17:34.216 --> 00:17:35.696
[groans]

00:17:35.739 --> 00:17:37.480
Ah, apparently,
we just missed K'orin.

00:17:37.524 --> 00:17:39.352
-If we hurry,
maybe we can get him.
-[sighs]

00:17:39.395 --> 00:17:41.136
-I don't even care anymore.
-What?

00:17:41.180 --> 00:17:43.443
-Oh, man, how much blood
did you lose?
-Ow. [sighs]

00:17:43.486 --> 00:17:45.271
This whole time, I've either
been one step behind you

00:17:45.314 --> 00:17:47.795
-or totally in the dark.
-Yeah, but only because
I'm pretty amazing.

00:17:47.838 --> 00:17:49.666
[sighs] Look,
everyone has bad days.

00:17:49.710 --> 00:17:51.364
All that studying,
and where did it get me?

00:17:51.407 --> 00:17:52.756
Klingon threw a knife
at my head.

00:17:52.800 --> 00:17:54.367
I nearly got eggs
laid in my throat.

00:17:54.410 --> 00:17:56.760
Those guys at the bar
wanted to eat me.

00:17:56.804 --> 00:17:58.066
What is that?
What are you doing?

00:17:58.110 --> 00:17:59.894
Kitalia leaves--
they contain a numbing agent.

00:17:59.937 --> 00:18:02.375
I've never once seen you study,but then you just

00:18:02.418 --> 00:18:04.464
breeze in here
knowing cool plant tricks

00:18:04.507 --> 00:18:06.030
and which aliens
are which-- how?

00:18:06.074 --> 00:18:07.380
Dude, I told you
I've been places.

00:18:07.423 --> 00:18:08.946
I just pick stuff up
along the way.

00:18:08.990 --> 00:18:10.252
I could never do that.

00:18:10.296 --> 00:18:12.211
I guess I'm just not cut out
for Starfleet.

00:18:12.254 --> 00:18:13.647
Oh, please,
you're Mr. Starfleet.

00:18:13.690 --> 00:18:15.127
No, I'm not, not like you are!

00:18:15.170 --> 00:18:17.172
I should just turn in
my uniform and go

00:18:17.216 --> 00:18:19.218
-work on a research asteroid!
-[gasps]

00:18:19.261 --> 00:18:21.785
No, absolutely not.
Do not even joke about that.

00:18:21.829 --> 00:18:23.222
That is the lamest thing
you could do.

00:18:23.265 --> 00:18:25.485
[crying]: I should just
study bugs on a far-off planet

00:18:25.528 --> 00:18:28.836
and then eventually get eaten
and no one will even know

00:18:28.879 --> 00:18:30.751
until they stumble
across my distress call,

00:18:30.794 --> 00:18:32.187
but it'll be way too late,

00:18:32.231 --> 00:18:33.754
and then they'll have to spend
a bunch of time

00:18:33.797 --> 00:18:35.234
deciphering
how things went wrong

00:18:35.277 --> 00:18:37.453
based on my final
shaky video logs.

00:18:37.497 --> 00:18:40.195
I'm sure you wouldn't get eaten.

00:18:40.239 --> 00:18:43.198
Starfleet doesn't just need
badass cool people like me.

00:18:43.242 --> 00:18:45.548
They need, like, book-smart
people like you, too.

00:18:45.592 --> 00:18:48.203
When we get back, I'm done.

00:18:48.247 --> 00:18:49.596
[grunts]

00:18:52.860 --> 00:18:54.905
All right, everyone, huddle up.

00:18:54.949 --> 00:18:58.735
I want to introduce you to the
newest bear in our bear pack.

00:18:58.779 --> 00:19:01.129
Rutherford's blood runs
yellow and black.

00:19:01.173 --> 00:19:03.000
He's one of us.

00:19:03.044 --> 00:19:05.394
Security isn't like
the other departments.

00:19:05.438 --> 00:19:07.918
[voice fading]:
No, it's a higher calling.

00:19:07.962 --> 00:19:10.573
We stand shoulder to shoulder,
holding the line

00:19:10.617 --> 00:19:13.228
against dangers
known and unknown.

00:19:13.272 --> 00:19:14.795
[regular volume]:
No greater honor

00:19:14.838 --> 00:19:16.666
than to die
beside you in battle.

00:19:16.710 --> 00:19:20.148
Yes, Rutherford, you're
never going to have to see

00:19:20.192 --> 00:19:22.542
the inside
of a Jefferies tube again.

00:19:22.585 --> 00:19:23.804
Thank you, sir.

00:19:23.847 --> 00:19:26.546
This all sounds fun
but not for me.

00:19:26.589 --> 00:19:27.982
-[all gasp]
-What?

00:19:28.025 --> 00:19:29.244
My heart's in engineering.

00:19:29.288 --> 00:19:31.246
I'd like permission
to leave the bear pack.

00:19:31.290 --> 00:19:33.335
Rutherford, that is...

00:19:33.379 --> 00:19:34.554
outstanding!

00:19:34.597 --> 00:19:35.859
Got to be true to yourself!

00:19:35.903 --> 00:19:37.252
-Am I right, bears?
-[all cheering]

00:19:37.296 --> 00:19:39.863
-Hoorah!
-Aw, bears.

00:19:41.387 --> 00:19:42.344
Come on, we got to take
a shortcut.

00:19:42.388 --> 00:19:43.345
We're almost out of time.

00:19:43.389 --> 00:19:44.433
Whatever. Who cares?

00:19:44.477 --> 00:19:45.565
I clearly do.

00:19:45.608 --> 00:19:47.349
Greetings, "hyoo-mons."

00:19:47.393 --> 00:19:49.656
I noticed you are injured.

00:19:49.699 --> 00:19:52.528
Perhaps I could
provide you transport.

00:19:52.572 --> 00:19:54.095
Uh, no, thank you, sir.

00:19:54.138 --> 00:19:55.531
[quietly]: Yeah, right.
Can you believe this guy?

00:19:55.575 --> 00:19:56.706
Actually, yeah,
that would be great.

00:19:56.750 --> 00:19:58.273
-We're kind of in a hurry.
-Wait, what?

00:19:58.317 --> 00:20:01.102
Excellent. My shuttle is
just beyond that ridge.

00:20:01.145 --> 00:20:03.452
Come, come.

00:20:03.496 --> 00:20:05.280
What are you doing?
We can't trust a Ferengi.

00:20:05.324 --> 00:20:07.239
-What? He's not a Ferengi.
-Yes, he is!

00:20:07.282 --> 00:20:09.197
-No, I think he's a Bolian.
-Oh, my God!

00:20:09.241 --> 00:20:12.113
He could not be more Ferengi--
the big ears, the beady eyes,

00:20:12.156 --> 00:20:13.288
that greedy thing they do
with their hands.

00:20:13.332 --> 00:20:15.159
"Hyoo-mon."

00:20:15.203 --> 00:20:16.726
-Myah.
-Ferengi are

00:20:16.770 --> 00:20:18.424
the most untrustworthy race
in the galaxy.

00:20:18.467 --> 00:20:20.730
He probably just wants to lureus over there so he can mug us.

00:20:20.774 --> 00:20:22.036
Look, we need a ride now,

00:20:22.079 --> 00:20:23.690
and my gut is telling me
this is fine.

00:20:23.733 --> 00:20:25.866
Need I remind you
that you've been wrong

00:20:25.909 --> 00:20:27.476
about literally
everything today?

00:20:27.520 --> 00:20:28.869
Not this.

00:20:28.912 --> 00:20:30.305
Uh-huh, sure. Okay, buddy.

00:20:30.349 --> 00:20:31.828
-Let's go.
-Good, good.

00:20:31.872 --> 00:20:34.353
-Follow me right this...
-What's your landing code?

00:20:34.396 --> 00:20:35.571
Uh, what?

00:20:35.615 --> 00:20:37.312
Tulganan security requires
all shuttlecraft

00:20:37.356 --> 00:20:39.096
to provide
a secure landing code.

00:20:39.140 --> 00:20:41.490
If you really have a shuttle
here, you must have a code.

00:20:41.534 --> 00:20:43.057
Oh, my code, yes.

00:20:43.100 --> 00:20:45.320
It's, uh, right... here!

00:20:45.364 --> 00:20:46.974
-Give me your profit!
-Oh!

00:20:47.017 --> 00:20:48.323
[grunts]

00:20:48.367 --> 00:20:50.456
Aah! Starfleet!

00:20:50.499 --> 00:20:51.761
Hey, Ferengi,
get-get out of here!

00:20:51.805 --> 00:20:52.980
Get! Get!

00:20:53.023 --> 00:20:55.330
Okay, maybe you were right.
That, uh...

00:20:55.374 --> 00:20:56.940
that seems like that
might've been a Ferengi.

00:20:56.984 --> 00:20:59.813
I was soright, yes!
[grunts, gasps]

00:20:59.856 --> 00:21:02.076
Holy crap, it's the shuttle.
It's the shuttle!

00:21:03.077 --> 00:21:04.948
-Bye-bye.
-Isn't that illegal?

00:21:04.992 --> 00:21:06.863
What are they gonna do,
send me a bill in space?

00:21:06.907 --> 00:21:08.909
Fair enough. If we gun it, we
can just make it back in time.

00:21:08.952 --> 00:21:11.390
-[snoring]
-Oh, man, he drank everything!

00:21:11.433 --> 00:21:12.782
-What do we do?
-Grab a leg.

00:21:12.826 --> 00:21:14.349
Let's drag him outand leave him by the front door,

00:21:14.393 --> 00:21:16.133
unless you don't think
that's Starfleet enough.

00:21:16.177 --> 00:21:17.787
It isn't, but let's do it.

00:21:20.747 --> 00:21:22.357
K'ORIN:
I demand

00:21:22.401 --> 00:21:24.316
you give me an honorable...

00:21:24.359 --> 00:21:26.187
[retches]

00:21:26.230 --> 00:21:28.450
[sighs]
Someone contact the Cerritos,

00:21:28.494 --> 00:21:30.234
tell them
we finally found K'orin.

00:21:30.278 --> 00:21:32.541
He is just in time
for the peace accords.

00:21:32.585 --> 00:21:34.848
Fetch me my drinking horn.
I need ale.

00:21:34.891 --> 00:21:37.329
Are you [bleep] kidding me?
No! Stop that.

00:21:40.462 --> 00:21:41.898
Whew, what a day!

00:21:41.942 --> 00:21:44.248
Man, that escort missionkind of went off the rails, huh?

00:21:44.292 --> 00:21:46.033
Sure did.

00:21:46.076 --> 00:21:48.992
Can't believe I didn't realizethat was a Ferengi in the park.

00:21:49.036 --> 00:21:50.385
[laughs, sighs]

00:21:50.429 --> 00:21:52.474
Hey, uh, so do you think maybe,

00:21:52.518 --> 00:21:54.781
maybe, fun idea, we could
just keep it between us?

00:21:54.824 --> 00:21:56.565
For sure.
We're in a circle of trust.

00:21:56.609 --> 00:21:58.785
This is a shuttle of silence.

00:21:58.828 --> 00:22:00.787
-[laughter]
-So the Ferengi's right there,

00:22:00.830 --> 00:22:02.745
and I'm like, "Mariner,
we can't trust this guy.

00:22:02.789 --> 00:22:04.791
He's a Ferengi." And then
she says, she says, get this,

00:22:04.834 --> 00:22:07.184
she says,
"Oh, no, that's a Bolian."

00:22:07.228 --> 00:22:09.404
[laughter]

00:22:09.448 --> 00:22:11.406
-Bolian!
-Okay, okay.

00:22:11.450 --> 00:22:13.016
Yep, yep, all right.

00:22:13.060 --> 00:22:15.323
After this long day
of being a badass,

00:22:15.367 --> 00:22:17.151
Captain Know-It-All over here
doesn't even know

00:22:17.194 --> 00:22:19.327
-what a Ferengi was.
-It wasn't as clear as that.

00:22:19.371 --> 00:22:21.982
[impersonating Ferengi]:
"Myah, myah, hyoo-mon!"

00:22:22.025 --> 00:22:23.853
He was doing the hand thing
and everything.

00:22:23.897 --> 00:22:25.202
All right, yeah,
no, that's my cue

00:22:25.246 --> 00:22:27.335
to go just launch myself
out an air lock.

00:22:27.379 --> 00:22:29.119
You guys have a great night.

00:22:29.163 --> 00:22:31.121
Lucky I was there!
I spotted it. I called it.

00:22:31.165 --> 00:22:33.167
-I called it.
-[laughter]

00:22:34.908 --> 00:22:36.126
Tendi, I'm sorry.

00:22:36.170 --> 00:22:37.780
I tried to make it work
in another division.

00:22:37.824 --> 00:22:40.130
I just couldn't do it.
I belong in the tubes.

00:22:40.174 --> 00:22:42.829
-I'm not gonna be able
to watch the pulsar with you.
-All right, whatever.

00:22:42.872 --> 00:22:44.526
I'll just watch it
in there with you on my PADD.

00:22:44.570 --> 00:22:45.919
Wait, you can?
We don't have to go

00:22:45.962 --> 00:22:47.355
to the observation deck
or anything?

00:22:47.399 --> 00:22:48.922
Nah, I just wanted company.
[laughs]

00:22:48.965 --> 00:22:51.359
I mean, it's not like you were
trying all those new jobs

00:22:51.403 --> 00:22:52.665
just to hang with me, right?

00:22:52.708 --> 00:22:55.319
[laughing]
No, yeah, no.

00:22:55.363 --> 00:22:57.060
Could you imagine?

00:22:59.106 --> 00:23:00.412
[tablet beeping]

00:23:00.455 --> 00:23:03.502
Ah, Mariner, was I
convincing enough for you,

00:23:03.545 --> 00:23:05.808
"hyoo-mon"? [laughs]

00:23:05.852 --> 00:23:08.115
You were perfect, Quimp.
Thanks for helping out.

00:23:08.158 --> 00:23:09.551
Of course. I owed you one.

00:23:09.595 --> 00:23:11.335
-How's the wife?
-She's good.

00:23:11.379 --> 00:23:13.947
We're actually looking to
get away to Risa this weekend.

00:23:13.990 --> 00:23:15.992
What? Ah, jealous.

00:23:16.036 --> 00:23:19.082
Oh, you know what you guys
should try? Jamaharon.

00:23:21.128 --> 00:23:22.172
Wow.

00:23:22.216 --> 00:23:23.739
Isn't it amazing?

00:23:23.783 --> 00:23:24.784
[sighs]

00:23:24.827 --> 00:23:27.177
It's beautiful.

00:23:29.136 --> 00:23:33.096
